WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.020
- So, what's going to happen

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.400
with the second impeachment trial

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.190
of former President Donald Trump?

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.850
Well, at this point, it's
sort of anyone's guess.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.140
Because, remember, the
Senate basically negotiates

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.750
the rules every time they do it.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.870
And in this case, something
really weird is going on,

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.100
because Chief Justice of the
Supreme Court John Roberts

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.100
is not going to preside over the trial.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.570
Instead, it's going to be
democratic Senator Patrick Leahy.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:19.550
And that seems weird,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.440
because the Constitution
seems to contemplate

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.910
the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.950
Now, experts disagree,

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:25.580
but in the case of a former president,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.980
it's not entirely clear that
the Supreme Court justice

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.360
must actually preside.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.720
And since the Senate
is basically making up

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.970
the rules as they go along,
it's probably going to be okay,

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.380
and frankly, it would
be a political question

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.280
if anyone tried to challenge
it in court anyway.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.090
So, we'll see what happens
with this new impeachment,

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.683
and I'll see you in court.

